A||||5||My7Fieros||OOPS!! What did I do?||||11||
Z||000000||My7Fieros||10-22-2000||07:35 PM||||Well I took the Formula to one of those do it yourself carwashes...cleaned her up real good. HOWEVER, I power washed the engine..Ive done it before (on other Fieros, first time for this one). After washing, I pulled out onto the street where the check engine light came on..only for maybe 5 seconds then it went off (and hasnt come back on since). I made a left turn and drove maybe 300 feet and came to a red light (one of the longest on the planet) and the car kinda started surging ...the tach needle jerked from 1000 to 1100 some..then stalled! I started back up, put in gear, stalled. I started back up, put in gear, and drove off without a problem. <BR>I suspect something that shouldntve gotten wet got wet...am I right, and if so, what? Thanx||||reg||11
Z||000001||Seanh||10-22-2000||08:34 PM||||Sounds like somthing to do with the ignition system. You could have maybe gotten water under the dist. cap, or under the plug wires attaching to the cap, or coil. This happens to me on some other cars, but never the Fiero. Check to see what code the engine light left on the computer, maybe it will help.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||10-22-2000||09:58 PM||||It only showed the code once, and only for a couple of seconds..it hasnt come on since.<BR>I figured something just got wet that shouldnt have. After that one incodent it did fine. I let it sit at home for a few hours while I went out to eat (in another car). When I got home just now I drove it around the block a few times...did fine, no prob.<BR>Guess I just to be more cognisent of where Im spraying 50 psi of water next time I hose down the engine! But shes doing fine now, just got me nervous!<BR>Man, these things are skiddish!<BR>Thanx though!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Brian||||reg||1
Z||000003||BAM-BAM||10-22-2000||10:19 PM||||   Check your computer code. It will tell you what set off the check engine light<P>  Later, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach Springs/KYB shocks and struts<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats, Carpet and headliner! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||1
Z||000004||StuGood||10-22-2000||11:26 PM||||Tach jumps?  Engine stalls?  When wet?<BR>I say it was the tach filter got wet<BR>(Stu's favorite answer for everything).<P>e.g. - Headaches? Flat feet? Can't get girls to go out with you? - Tach filter!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||3
Z||000005||Seanh||10-22-2000||11:44 PM||||Yeah, I have noticed you seem to like the tach filter solution alot. If anyones noticed me, I seem to like the cracked EGR tube, running from the bottem of the intake to the EGR valve, solution for alot of things.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
